---
// NEW post (v3): fuse board warning signs. Direct answer first, the 7
// signs, the honest bit about plastic boards, 2026 costs. Copy from COPY.md.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { client } from '../../data/client.js';

const tel = client.phone.replace(/\s/g, '');
const article = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Fuse board upgrade: 7 signs yours is due, and 2026 costs',
  datePublished: '2026-07-29',
  dateModified: '2026-07-29',
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: client.owner, jobTitle: 'Electrician' },
  publisher: { '@id': 'https://eselec.co.uk/#business' },
};
const breadcrumbs = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
  itemListElement: [
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://eselec.co.uk/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Blog', item: 'https://eselec.co.uk/blog/' },
    { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: 'Fuse board upgrade signs', item: 'https://eselec.co.uk/blog/fuse-board-upgrade-signs/' },
  ],
};

const SIGNS = [
  ['Fuse wire', 'If blown fuses get mended with wire from a card, the board predates every protection standard your family currently relies on.'],
  ['No test button anywhere', 'No RCD. On a fault, that’s the difference between milliseconds and a serious shock.'],
  ['Scorch marks or a warm, fishy smell at the board', 'That’s a connection cooking itself. Ring someone this week, not this quarter.'],
  ['One trip kills the whole house', 'A single shared RCD means one faulty kettle blacks out the freezer, the alarm and the wifi. Modern boards give every circuit its own.'],
  ['Buzzing or crackling', 'Boards should be silent. Noise is arcing, and arcing is how board fires start.'],
  ['No spare ways', 'Planning an EV charger, an extension or an electric shower? A full board can’t take the circuit.'],
  ['A wooden backboard', 'Pre-1970s, and usually accompanied by rubber or fabric-insulated cable somewhere in the house. Budget for an EICR before the board swap, because the board might be the good news.'],
];
---
<Base
  title="Fuse Board Upgrade: 7 Signs and 2026 Costs"
  description="A fuse board replacement costs £520 to £850 in Leeds in 2026. A working electrician lists the 7 signs yours is due, and the honest truth about plastic boards."
  current="/blog/"
  schema={[article, breadcrumbs]}
>
  <article class="paper">
    <div class="wrap article">
      <header class="article__head">
        <h1>Fuse board upgrade: 7 signs yours is due, and 2026 costs</h1>
        <p class="article__meta">
          By {client.owner}, electrician, ES Elec · July 2026 <!-- TEMP author -->
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="article__body">
        <p>
          A fuse board (consumer unit) replacement costs £520 to £850 fitted
          in Leeds in 2026 <!-- TEMP -->, takes a day, and the power is off
          for about six hours of it. Here are the seven signs the box on
          your wall has had its time, from a bloke who swaps one most weeks.
        </p>

        <h2>The 7 signs</h2>
        <ol class="signs">
          {SIGNS.map(([sign, detail]) => (
            <li>
              <strong>{sign}:</strong> {detail}
            </li>
          ))}
        </ol>

        <h2>The honest bit about plastic boards</h2>
        <p>
          Plastic consumer units are not illegal and yours might be fine.
          The question that matters is whether every circuit has RCD
          protection and whether the connections are sound. A photo answers
          half of that on the phone, free.
        </p>

        <h2>What a swap costs in 2026</h2>
        <p>
          Straight swap, 6 ways: £520 to £650. 10 ways with surge
          protection: £650 to £850. Bonding upgrades where gas and water
          were never done: add £120 to £250. <!-- TEMP figures --> Every
          price includes testing each circuit as it reconnects, and the
          certificate.
        </p>

        <h2>What happens on the day</h2>
        <p>
          Power goes off mid-morning and stays off for about six hours: keep
          the fridge shut and it holds. The old unit comes out, the new
          board goes in with RCBO protection per circuit, every circuit gets
          tested as it reconnects, the ways get labels that name what
          actually runs on them, and the certificate is in your hand before
          the van leaves. You get the off-time the day before, so the
          wifi-and-laptop question is sorted in advance.
        </p>

        <div class="band">
          <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem;">Recognise your board above?</h2>
          <p style="color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: var(--t-small);">
            A photo of your board gets you a price range on the same call.
          </p>
          <div class="acts">
            <a class="btn btn--call" href={`tel:${tel}`}>Call Eddie</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .signs { padding-left: 0; list-style: none; counter-reset: sign; display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .signs li { counter-increment: sign; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 34px 1fr; gap: 12px; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .signs li::before {
    content: counter(sign);
    font: 700 1rem var(--font-display);
    color: var(--accent);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--edge);
    border-radius: 50%;
    width: 30px; height: 30px;
    display: grid; place-items: center;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .signs strong { color: var(--ink); }
</style>
